From 56918884d93faf4e0fc6434b6319e2a482cb8471 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Lepikhov <andrei.lepikhov@pgedge.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 13:38:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix log threshold checks in emit-log hook (PG19 and
 comparison direction)

Two defects in the filter that replaced the pg18-020-LOG-to-DEBUG1
core patch, both in the block that re-evaluates message visibility
after demoting the retry messages from LOG to DEBUG1:

1. PostgreSQL 19 changed the log_min_messages GUC from a plain int
   into an int array indexed by backend type (see
   is_log_level_output() and its callers in
   src/backend/utils/error/elog.c).  The old comparison therefore
   compared the array pointer against the error level on PG19 and
   later, yielding an arbitrary result.  Use
   log_min_messages[MyBackendType] under PG_VERSION_NUM >= 190000;
   miscadmin.h is already included.

2. The comparisons had their operands swapped on all PG versions:
   'log_min_messages < edata->elevel' suppresses output when the
   threshold is *more* verbose than the message.  In practice, with
   the default log_min_messages = WARNING the demoted message was
   still written to the server log (just relabelled DEBUG1), so the
   filter silenced nothing by default, while lowering the threshold
   to DEBUG5 for debugging suppressed the messages instead.  The
   correct check is 'edata->elevel < threshold'.  A plain numeric
   comparison matches core's is_log_level_output() for every
   threshold value here because the demoted level DEBUG1 sorts below
   LOG.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/spock.c | 16 +++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/spock.c b/src/spock.c
index 0d23c2f..5937794 100644
--- a/src/spock.c
+++ b/src/spock.c
@@ -988,10 +988,20 @@ log_message_filter(ErrorData *edata)
 
 		if (lower_output_level)
 		{
-			/* Reconsider decision on exposing the message */
-			if (log_min_messages < edata->elevel)
+			/*
+			 * Reconsider the errstart() decision on exposing the message,
+			 * this time for the demoted level.  A plain comparison is
+			 * enough to mirror is_log_level_output() here because the
+			 * demoted level DEBUG1 sorts below LOG, so the LOG special
+			 * cases coincide with the numeric order.
+			 */
+#if PG_VERSION_NUM >= 190000
+			if (edata->elevel < log_min_messages[MyBackendType])
+#else
+			if (edata->elevel < log_min_messages)
+#endif
 				edata->output_to_server = false;
-			if (client_min_messages < edata->elevel)
+			if (edata->elevel < client_min_messages)
 				edata->output_to_client = false;
 		}
 	}
